Pass a variadic call's anonymous arguments as anonymous

The function type a call goes through listed every argument as a
parameter, so GCC passed the anonymous ones as named.  Where the target
passes them differently (on the C33 every anonymous argument is on the
stack), the callee's va_arg read the wrong words.  The type now lists the
named arguments only.

